    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0277" n="207" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2968: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-12T13:00:00+00:00"
                            >December 12, 1918—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. From Grew. Will you please request the consuls throughout the Allied and
                    neutral countries and those countries bordering the Mediterranean to transmit to
                    the American Mission copies of recent and all future reports dealing with the
                    political situation or with any economic situation of sufficient magnitude to
                    have political significance. This request is made in order that we may have at
                    hand here the information on which to predicate comments, criticisms and the
                    like in regard to existing conditions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>] <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
